.br
int \fBgf_sftp_client_rmdir\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *path, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
.br
int \fBgf_sftp_client_realpath\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *path, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
.br
int \fBgf_sftp_client_rename\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *from, const char *to, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
.br
int \fBgf_sftp_client_readlink\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *path, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
LENGTH is the most the answer may carry; it must fit the packet size.
.TP
int \fBgf_sftp_client_symlink\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *linkpath, const char *target, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
.br
int \fBgf_sftp_client_extended\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *name, const uint8_t *data, size_t len, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
Make LINKPATH a link to TARGET.  On the wire the target comes first, as OpenSSH and the implementations that follow it do, which is the reverse of what the draft text says; a server request has the link in path and the target in path2 whichever way they came.
.TP
int \fBgf_sftp_client_extension\fP (const gf_sftp_client *c, const char *name, gf_slice *data);
What the server advertised in its VERSION: 1 and its data if it did (valid until the client is freed), else 0.
.TP
int \fBgf_sftp_client_posix_rename\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *from, const char *to, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
.br
int \fBgf_sftp_client_statvfs\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *path, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
.br
int \fBgf_sftp_client_fstatvfs\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const uint8_t *handle, size_t hl, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
Requests of the extensions.  Each is GF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED if the server did not advertise the extension.  The answer is a STATUS, except that statvfs, fstatvfs and limits are answered with an EXTENDED_REPLY (gf_sftp_response_statvfs, _limits), expand_path with a NAME of one entry, and users_groups_by_id with an EXTENDED_REPLY (gf_sftp_response_users_groups).
.TP
int \fBgf_sftp_client_hardlink\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *oldpath, const char *newpath, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
.br
int \fBgf_sftp_client_fsync\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const uint8_t *handle, size_t hl, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
Make NEWPATH another name for the file OLDPATH.
.TP
int \fBgf_sftp_client_lsetstat\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *path, const gf_sftp_attrs *attrs, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
.br
int \fBgf_sftp_client_limits\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
Like setstat, but of a symbolic link itself.
.TP
int \fBgf_sftp_client_expand_path\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const char *path, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
Expand a path that begins with "~" or "~user" on the server.
.TP
int \fBgf_sftp_client_copy_data\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const uint8_t *read_handle, size_t rhl, uint64_t offset, uint64_t length, const uint8_t *write_handle, size_t whl, uint64_t offset2, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
Copy LENGTH bytes (0: to the end) from OFFSET of the file READ_HANDLE to OFFSET2 of WRITE_HANDLE on the server, without them passing through the client.
.TP
int \fBgf_sftp_client_users_groups_by_id\fP (gf_sftp_client *c, const uint32_t *uids, size_t nuids, const uint32_t *gids, size_t ngids, void *tag, uint32_t *id);
The names of NUIDS user ids and NGIDS group ids (each at most GF_SFTP_MAX_IDS).
